 sound\" and he's \"really proud of how it turned out\"; Calvin: \"Wow, Dave! You really turned it into a masterpiece. Impressive!\" [S22T3][S22T4].\n- On 2023-10-25, shared a photo of his latest car project (a group of people washing a car in a garage); Calvin: \"that car looks awesome!\" and asked what got him into engineering cars [S26T4][S26T5].\n- On 2023-10-25, when asked (by Calvin) what got him into engineering cars, gave a second, complementary origin story: cars have \"always been [his] thing\" — his dad took him to his first car show when he was 10, he was \"wow-ed,\" and \"I was hooked and wanted to learn more\"; now he's an automotive engineer, and it's \"crazy to think that something so powerful and cool can be made from small parts\" (complements the 2023-10-23 origin story — fascination with machines at ten and the neighbor's old car — in the Hobbies and sense of purpose section of this file; Calvin: \"So happy you followed your dreams and became an engineer. Seeing you work on cars is inspiring - it makes me want to keep pushing my music.\") [S26T6][S26T7].\n- On 2023-10-25, Calvin: \"I'm totally into cars too and love making new and powerful models\" — a shared car passion (Calvin's side in the Music section of /memories/calvin.md) [S26T5].\n- On 2023-10-29, when Calvin asked how the car project was going, told him \"The car project is doing well\" — he \"just finished restoring it and it looks amazing\" — and invited Calvin over to check it out (\"Wanna come by and check it out?\") (Calvin: \"That's awesome, Dave! Your car project sounds amazing.\"); the restoration is of the current/latest car project he shared on 2023-10-25 (photo of people washing a car in a garage) — i.e., the new, challenging black-car project he mentioned on 2023-10-23 (see above) [S27T9][S27T10].","text_sha256":"27fa4200d9f2c8eeb9141b238448ba4a73af82d7c21d2d8e7114f38c8cd85aff","timestamp":null},{"attribution_index_sha256":"98109144a5a23da7a5b89634be2c543ea2366f2abe85f1f3f8a