104de483abe8f21d237335ae655022af895a5c6898618498e19d92ad07","speaker":"Dave","turn_index":17},{"dia_id":"D25:18","global_turn_index":442,"locator":"[S25T18]","raw_turn_sha256":"1e1814948edbcd3ad0641146b727b68d78dfd7153ae8ce6e9cc9c1e4753e3544","rendered_turn_sha256":"a5c581070e44d6a099f9f90cc521dba6695f64fdb0cc281e525abbb29a638c02","session_date":"2023-10-23","session_datetime":"2023-10-23T14:17:00","session_id":"session_25","session_index":25,"source_sha256":"69fddda49b1d63bb583eeb59246471eebbe7d914d3b9b4df1060d807a049f499","speaker":"Calvin","turn_index":18},{"dia_id":"D25:19","global_turn_index":443,"locator":"[S25T19]","raw_turn_sha256":"fea632cb4aaca1a6cb8ceba50d6fa8e5b99b9b589b11f38608a84bfeee780138","rendered_turn_sha256":"3f0538f91565163c8cbc8682334fbf42f4ae001a382069b04e82b05dbfc03c93","session_date":"2023-10-23","session_datetime":"2023-10-23T14:17:00","session_id":"session_25","session_index":25,"source_sha256":"14bb3c4bc2e75bf5c476cd677c32624cd7dc79c6d76c6407ccac5b28d6cc9384","speaker":"Dave","turn_index":19},{"dia_id":"D26:4","global_turn_index":459,"locator":"[S26T4]","raw_turn_sha256":"e52a41492e27f76b0a253869d64d8cb7986acbead14b8a53b99d3ef110a7c145","rendered_turn_sha256":"36b999a0e53408c35fe6829785843f67e2e66149e833930c0fa94c11ef53eb38","session_date":"2023-10-25","session_datetime":"2023-10-25T20:25:00","session_id":"session_26","session_index":26,"source_sha256":"afee282a44f4a93fb58775508faf28ecd1d0a9c174ee812426cdbf5ee6f9c091","speaker":"Dave","turn_index":4}],"speaker":null,"store_id":"s3","store_snapshot_sha256":"983238fddc77a88ef4ae3d06b50bcfd25a429f497e89c6af4d9477cefca9cad2","text":"- Gets \"a real buzz\" transforming something that's not working into something that runs smoothly — \"like giving it a second chance\" [S7T6].\n- Giving something a new life \"makes [him] feel powerful and happy — like [he] really achieved something\"; he agreed with Calvin that they both \"take something and make it look amazing\" [S7T7][S7T8].\n- On 2023-08-03, said fixing cars is like therapy for him; growing up he worked on cars with his dad, and refurbishing them gives him a sense of fulfillment [S12T2].\n- On 2023-09-02, when telling Calvin he's been tied up with car stuff, said fixing stuff up and seeing it turn out better is \"really rewarding and gives me a sense of purpose\", and that fixing someone's car makes him feel like he's \"making a difference\"; he's made \"proud\" to see the relief on someone's face when their car is fixed (echoing his long-stated sense of purpose from fixing things, see above) [S17T3][S17T5].\n- Has fond memories of working on cars with his dad as a kid: they spent one summer restoring an old car — \"It was hard work, but seeing the end result and knowing that we did it together was really satisfying\" [S12T4].\n- Shared a photo from that time: a man and a child (Dave and his dad) posing for a picture — \"a wonderful experience\" [S12T6].\n- On 2023-09-15, told Calvin (answering whether it's satisfying to see his hard work pay off, on the restoration finished that day — context in ## Car mod workshop (2023-08-11)) that \"It's so satisfying to see this brought back to life,\" especially seeing people's reactions when they see the finished product — \"makes all the hard work worth it\" [S19T9].\n- On 2023-10-04, said he loves being able to transform something old and beat-up into something beautiful, and that it's the small successes that make him feel proud and fulfilled (said to Calvin right after Calvin praised his grease-stained hands — \"Those hands show you worked hard. You put in lots of effort. You should definitely be proud!\" — context in ## Car mod workshop (2023-08-11)) [S21T10].\n- On 2023-10-08, when telling Calvin about his car show and restored/modified car (details in ## Classic cars), said working on cars \"is not just a hobby, it's a passion\" — it's \"like therapy, a way to get away from everyday stress\"; as a kid he'd spend hours in his dad's garage, tinkering with engines — \"it was like my own sanctuary\" (echoing his childhood memories of working on cars with his dad, see above); now he's \"lucky enough to do this as a job, to take something broken and make it into something awesome\" [S22T5].\n- On 2023-10-08, said doing what he loves has been \"my goal since I was a kid\" and it's awesome that he's able to do it; restoring things can be tough but \"the feeling of accomplishment it gives is great\"; Calvin responded that bringing broken things back to life is \"so satisfying,\" that working on cars \"can be a real escape from reality\" (he understands the feeling), and that \"doing what you love for a living, that's the ultimate goal,\" adding \"Keep going with it, it's really inspiring.\" [S22T5][S22T6][S22T7].\n- On 2023-10-23, told Calvin he recently had a good conversation with some neighbors about current events and politics — it was nice to hear different perspectives and share their own; he finds that interacting like that cheers him up and helps him stay informed (conversation flow in the 2023-10-23 entry of ## Relationships; Calvin's response in the Music and Relationships sections of /memories/calvin.md) [S25T7].\n- On 2023-10-23, told Calvin (who asked \"what made you start working on cars?\") that his car passion started when he was ten: he'd been fascinated with how machines work, found an old car in a neighbor's garage, and asked if he could fix it — \"that's when my love for car engineering began!\" — he enjoyed transforming it from broken-down to high-running, and that sense of accomplishment made him hooked, so he's been working on cars ever since (shared a photo of a man working on a car in a garage; comes with his remark that working on a car is his outlet — \"a little oasis of calm\" — where he's \"connecting back with myself\" — see the 2023-10-23 entry of ## Relationships; complements the childhood memories of tinkering with engines in his dad's garage recorded above; Calvin: \"Impressive! That must have taken a lot of skill and determination to bring that car back to life.\", and asked whether it was a classic car and whether Dave still has it or is working on another project — Dave answered in the continuation of the same day's chat, which is not in this excerpt: he restored a car last year (2022, the 2022 restoration, see above) but sold it to a collector, and is now working on a new car project he finds quite a challenge [S25T14][S25T15][S25T16][S25T17].\n- On 2023-10-23, told Calvin (who asked what the toughest part of car restoration is) that it takes a lot of patience but the payoff is worth it, and paying extra attention to detail isn't easy but it pays off — echoing his earlier remarks that small details make his mod project unique and personalized (details in ## Car mod workshop (2023-08-11)) and that the small successes make him proud (see above) [S25T18][S25T19].\n- On 2023-10-25, said working on a car project \"takes me out of my head and calms me down\" — complementing his long-stated \"oasis of calm\"/therapy remarks above [S26T4].","text_sha256":"adb496c7af3f213d849586dac00f7ddd6774025516245ad6076dd845de3456c6","timestamp":null}],"integrity":{"post_tree_sha256":"983238fddc77a88ef4ae3d06b50bcfd25a429f497e89c6af4d9477cefca9cad2","pre_tree_sha256":"983238fddc77a88ef4ae3d06b50bcfd25a429f497e89c6af4d9477cefca9cad2","store_unchanged":true,"verified":true},"metrics":{"completion_tokens":1059,"filesystem_tool_calls":0,"model_calls":4,"orchestration_calls":4,"prompt_tokens":58614,"provider_request_attempts":4,"provider_rounds":4,"token_usage_available":true,"total_tokens":59673},"model":{"requested_model":"coding","served_models":["qwen3.8:27b"]},"prompt_contract":{"derived_prompt_sha256":"60d0c608bdda6e13c46a9e6cbf4cd7cae4f7eea8d7fcd2d8a4f8f9bde415df7c","filesystem_tools_sha256":"1632a476feccd761a1c6d21c9d2962d0975632f50d6c96678d69427a7f973ed7","orchestration_actions_sha256":"115512fb955e8c7fca557e4b995c5bfd8717ca72dfb184810b04343bc595cd08","paper_prompt_